# Makepad 2 only

- Use Makepad 2 APIs: `script_mod!`, `AppMain::script_mod`, `#[derive(Script, ScriptHook, Widget)]`, `app_main!`. Never Makepad 1 docs/examples/APIs (`live_design!`, `LiveHook`).
- `vendor/makepad` is generated by `./scripts/setup-makepad.sh` (pinned `MAKEPAD_REV` + `patches/makepad/` at `--fuzz=0`) and gitignored. Never edit it directly; change or add a patch, regenerated from a real before/after tree (`docs/DEV.md` § Changing a patch).
- Keep rev and patches identical to the other Gotigin workspaces; change them deliberately everywhere.
- Solid backgrounds: `SolidView { draw_bg +: {color: #x0d0b3a} }`. A plain `View { show_bg: true … }` paints nothing on this rev.
- Library widgets: `mod.widgets.<Name>Base = #(<Name>::register_widget(vm))` + `set_type_default() do …`, exposed through `pub fn script_mod(vm)`. Prefix script names with the crate name. Apps register them after `makepad_widgets::script_mod(vm)` and add `use mod.widgets.*`.
- Never block the UI thread: devices, network and disk work run on threads, and results come back as actions.
- UI work is not done until seen: screenshot under a private Xvfb on a free display, never `:0` or another session's display (`docs/DEV.md` § Look at the screen).
